From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: enable the USB-C
 analog headset

The Pad 4 has no 3.5 mm jack; stock plays analog headsets through the
USB-C port (qcom,msm-mbhc-usbc-audio-supported in its sound card): the
WCD9395 USBSS switch routes the codec's headphone and microphone lines to
the connector's D+/D- and SBU pins in Type-C audio accessory mode. The
codec and the switch are both described here, and the switch is already
the connector's SBU mux, but the two are not connected: the switch does
not find the codec's mode / orientation switch, so the codec's headset
detection is never told about an accessory.

Describe the codec as a mode and orientation switch and link it to the
switch's port@1, as the Kaanapali MTP does (Balaji Kalkonda, "arm64:
dts: qcom: kaanapali-mtp: Enable USB headset and Type-C accessory mode",
v2 4/5, Reviewed-by Konrad Dybcio). Also route MIC BIAS2 to AMIC2, the
codec's headset microphone input, as the other WCD939x boards do. The
MTP's I2C bus changes (100 kHz, internal 2.2 kOhm pull-up) are not
taken: without a clock-frequency this bus already runs at the GENI
controller's default of 100 kHz, and the switch answers on it today.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20261015-kaanapali_dp-v2-4-c15cb83d9140@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 24dd73c3e017b118b93de7c3f6b5d9aa2cf313ef)
---
 .../dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts     | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index d11551573..f184892ff 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -369,6 +369,7 @@ sound {
 		audio-routing = "IN1_HPHL", "HPHL_OUT",
 				"IN2_HPHR", "HPHR_OUT",
 				"AMIC1", "MIC BIAS1",
+				"AMIC2", "MIC BIAS2",
 				"AMIC5", "MIC BIAS1",
 				"TX SWR_INPUT0", "ADC1_OUTPUT",
 				"TX SWR_INPUT1", "ADC2_OUTPUT",
@@ -495,6 +496,15 @@ wcd939x: audio-codec {
 		vdd-px-supply = <&vreg_l1g_1p2>;
 
 		#sound-dai-cells = <1>;
+
+		mode-switch;
+		orientation-switch;
+
+		port {
+			wcd_codec_headset_in: endpoint {
+				remote-endpoint = <&wcd_usbss_headset_out>;
+			};
+		};
 	};
 
 	wcn7860-pmu {
@@ -1325,6 +1335,14 @@ wcd_usbss_sbu_mux: endpoint {
 					remote-endpoint = <&pmic_glink_sbu>;
 				};
 			};
+
+			port@1 {
+				reg = <1>;
+
+				wcd_usbss_headset_out: endpoint {
+					remote-endpoint = <&wcd_codec_headset_in>;
+				};
+			};
 		};
 	};
 };
